From e03fd927f7ead1f7d3cad7e139fce75934dd3765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:05:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX: scaling factor from the maximum absolute value

- the scaling factor of the right hand side is given by the maximum of
  the absolute values of its components, reduced on the device and over
  the processes: its norm underflows below about 1e-162 and overflows
  above about 1e154 (the solution was then zero, reported as converged)
- AmgXPCG in single precision refuses an absolute tolerance, which
  prevented the scaling (the scalar products of AmgX overflowed above
  about 1e19)
- documentation: statistics of the scaled system, tolerances given by
  AmgXParameters in single precision
- tests: right hand sides multiplied by 1e-158 and 1e158, right hand side
  of different scales on the processes, relative residuals computed on
  scaled vectors
---
